The answer you cannot check
At the top, the question asked: entries of a given kind, coded in a given
system, where the code is indexed but the system is not. On the left, matching
the code and quietly dropping the system: rows come back and they look exactly
right, which means a wider question has been answered without the caller being
able to tell. On the right, refusing instead, and naming which part is
supported and which qualifier is not.
